/*
Problem: Rotate Image
Platform: LeetCode (LC 48)
Topic: Matrix / In-Place Rotation

---------------------------------------------------------

Approach:

We need to rotate an n × n matrix
90 degrees clockwise in-place.

The challenge is:

- No extra matrix allowed.
- Modify the given matrix directly.

---------------------------------------------------------

Layer-by-Layer Rotation:

Think of the matrix as layers
(or rings).

Example:

1  2  3
4  5  6
7  8  9

Outer layer:

1 2 3
4   6
7 8 9

We rotate four elements at a time.

---------------------------------------------------------

4-Way Swap:

For a position:

(i, j)

Rotate:

Top    <- Left
Left   <- Bottom
Bottom <- Right
Right  <- Top

Coordinates:

Top:
(i, j)

Left:
(n-1-j, i)

Bottom:
(n-1-i, n-1-j)

Right:
(j, n-1-i)

---------------------------------------------------------

Swap Order:

Store top element first:

temp = matrix[i][j]

Then perform:

top    = left
left   = bottom
bottom = right
right  = temp

This completes one 90° clockwise rotation.

---------------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

1 2 3
4 5 6
7 8 9

After rotation:

7 4 1
8 5 2
9 6 3

---------------------------------------------------------

Layer Traversal:

Outer loop:

for each layer

    i = 0 to n/2 - 1

Inner loop:

Traverse elements of current layer:

    j = i to n-i-2

Rotate each group of four elements.

---------------------------------------------------------

Time Complexity: O(n²)

Every element is visited once.

Space Complexity: O(1)

Rotation is performed in-place.

---------------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:
    void rotate(vector<vector<int>>& matrix) {

        int n = matrix.size();

        // Process layer by layer
        for (int i = 0; i < n / 2; i++) {

            for (int j = i; j < n - i - 1; j++) {

                int temp = matrix[i][j];

                // Left -> Top
                matrix[i][j] =
                    matrix[n - 1 - j][i];

                // Bottom -> Left
                matrix[n - 1 - j][i] =
                    matrix[n - 1 - i][n - 1 - j];

                // Right -> Bottom
                matrix[n - 1 - i][n - 1 - j] =
                    matrix[j][n - 1 - i];

                // Top -> Right
                matrix[j][n - 1 - i] = temp;
            }
        }
    }
};
